<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">White Lotus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as White Lotus millenarianism</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The White Lotus was a Chinese religious tradition combining Buddhist and popular beliefs with expectations of the coming of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maitreya">Maitreya Buddha</a>. Its millenarian teachings inspired repeated rebellions against ruling dynasties. White Lotus ideas fed the Red Turban uprisings that helped bring down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-lotus-rebellion">White Lotus Rebellion</a> of 1796–1804 weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>.</p></div>
